# GitHub Actions deployment settings (never commit real credential values):
# Repository secret: CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
# Repository variable: CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
# Token requires permission to deploy this Worker and access its destination R2 bucket.
# Runtime R2 binding: BUCKET -> icvsp-requirements-workbook
# Canonical key: workbook/ICVSP_V-Cycle_Reviewed_Updated.xlsx
# Production UI and API share one origin; no frontend API URL or R2 secret is needed.
# Build selection is set automatically by pnpm build:cloudflare.
# Optional smoke-test origin, obtained from Wrangler deployment output:
# APP_PUBLIC_URL=https://actual-worker.actual-account.workers.dev
# Temporary migration setting on the OLD backend only:
# WORKBOOK_READ_ONLY=true
# Keep WORKBOOK_READ_ONLY unset on the new writable production backend.
